and the King and the Prince of Wales being not yet at loggerheads, there came on a visit to the English Court a certain prince, who was afterwards known to hi…”"},{"id":"sapt","name":"Sapt","aliases":["Colonel Sapt"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““This,” said he, “is Colonel Sapt, and I am called Fritz von Tarlenheim: we are both in the service of the King of Ruritania.””"},{"id":"black-michael","name":"Black Michael","aliases":["Michael","Duke Michael"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““We know Duke Michael,” said she.”"},{"id":"fritz-von-tarlenheim","name":"Fritz von Tarlenheim","aliases":["Fritz"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““This,” said he, “is Colonel Sapt, and I am called Fritz von Tarlenheim: we are both in the service of the King of Ruritania.””"},{"id":"rupert-hentzau","name":"Rupert Hentzau","aliases":["Rupert","Hentzau"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “I had enquiries made, and they’re all there--Lauengram, Krafstein, and young Rupert Hentzau: three rogues, too, on my honour, as fine as live in Ruritania.””"},{"id":"flavia","name":"Flavia","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: ““Because Princess Flavia said he grazed her cheek when he was graciously pleased to give her a cousinly kiss.”"},{"id":"antoinette-de-mauban","name":"Antoinette de Mauban","aliases":["Antoinette","Madame de Mauban"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “It was not hard to see that George’s references to the duke were intended to aggravate poor Bertram’s sufferings, so that I drew the inference that the duke had distinguished Madame de Mauban by his attentions.”"},{"id":"rudolf","name":"Rudolf","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““I wonder when in the world you’re going to do anything, Rudolf?”"},{"id":"johann","name":"Johann","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““Johann, the duke’s keeper.”"},{"id":"detchard","name":"Detchard","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: ““De Gautet, Bersonin, and Detchard.””"},{"id":"marshal-strakencz","name":"Marshal Strakencz","aliases":["Marshal"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: ““Marshal Strakencz,” whispered Sapt, and I knew that I was in the presence of the most famous veteran of the Ruritanian army.”"},{"id":"josef","name":"Josef","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““Well, is dinner ready, Josef?”"},{"id":"de-gautet","name":"De Gautet","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: ““De Gautet, Bersonin, and Detchard.””"},{"id":"princess-flavia","name":"Princess Flavia","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““All the world knows that Black Michael--well then, mother, the duke--would give his soul to marry his cousin, the Princess Flavia, and that she is to be the queen.””"},{"id":"bersonin","name":"Bersonin","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: ““De Gautet, Bersonin, and Detchard.””"},{"id":"rudolf-rassendyll","name":"Rudolf Rassendyll","aliases":["Mr. Rassendyll"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““I am Rudolf Rassendyll.”"},{"id":"george","name":"George","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Well then--and I must premise that I am going, perforce, to rake up the very scandal which my dear Lady Burlesdon wishes forgotten--in the year 1733, George II.”"},{"id":"robert","name":"Robert","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Besides her attractions, she possessed a large fortune, and my brother Robert was wise enough not to mind about her ancestry.”"},{"id":"palace","name":"Palace","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “For what relationship is there between Ruritania and Burlesdon, between the Palace at Strelsau or the Castle of Zenda and Number 305 Park Lane, W.?”"},{"id":"bertram","name":"Bertram","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “It struck me, however, that Bertram himself was absent and in low spirits, and when everybody except ourselves had gone, I rallied him on his moping preoccupation.”"},{"id":"george-featherly","name":"George Featherly","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “I called on George Featherly at the Embassy, and we had a bit of dinner together at Durand’s, and afterwards dropped in to the Opera; and after that we had a little supper, and after that we called on Bertram Bertrand…”"},{"id":"prefect","name":"Prefect","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “It was the custom that the Prefect of Police should send every afternoon a report to me on the condition of the capital and the feeling of the people: the document included also an account of the movements of any pers…”"},{"id":"chancellor","name":"Chancellor","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “Then came the Chancellor, for another three hours; and to him I had to explain that the hurt to my finger (we turned that bullet to happy account) prevented me from writing--whence arose great to-do, hunting of preced…”"},{"id":"krafstein","name":"Krafstein","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “I had enquiries made, and they’re all there--Lauengram, Krafstein, and young Rupert Hentzau: three rogues, too, on my honour, as fine as live in Ruritania.””"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"king","target":"palace","weight":7,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r2","source":"george","target":"king","weight":8,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":2,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r3","source":